{"title":"2006 SMT/Advanced Topics Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Advanced_Topics_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A college student is about to break up with her boyfriend, a mathematics major who is apparently more interested in math than her. Frustrated, she cries, ”You mathematicians have no soul! It’s all numbers and equations! What is the root of your incompetence?!” Her boyfriend assumes she means the square root of himself, or the square root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />. What two answers should he give?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Advanced_Topics_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Remember from <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euler%27s_identity\" title=\"Euler&#39;s identity\">Euler's Formula</a> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b95bf6b8c75da75931a4e41e66f24d8f5d9397c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta+i\\sin\\theta=e^{i\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"145\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b0c5f5dd9a7117afd9fec3eab210eed1d662f61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)+i\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=e^{\\pi i/2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"245\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbc6b49ec365e8a9022a8d00242d284b509484c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{i}=i^{1/2}=(e^{\\pi i/2})^{1/2}=e^{\\pi i/4}=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)+i\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+i\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"519\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Of course, we also have to consider the negative of this, so the two answers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e3f3c5597b11fbae5d7f878caa980abbac3d4ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+i\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-i\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"203\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Advanced_Topics_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are asked to find the “root” of the boyfriend and also \\(\\sqrt{i}\\).\n</p><p>---\n</p><p>Step 1: Square root of himself\n</p><p>Assume the boyfriend is represented by \\(1\\). Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/24123c4bee8d2b08446777cb96c4a278d30c20f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{1} = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad -1\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>---\n</p><p>Step 2: Square root of \\(i\\)\n</p><p>Let  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/565f6e15d1613d5846ce9c33aaed7a28d3be5e64.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{i} = a + bi, \\quad a, b \\in \\mathbb{R}\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Then  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/6/59609f5eb35f0b11da7075f5d0ae3cd5df4011e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a + bi)^2 = i \\implies a^2 - b^2 + 2ab i = 0 + 1i\\]\" width=\"325\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Equating real and imaginary parts:  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c2480e04dc54d6acf19c8fdaef04c04b6878123.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{cases} a^2 - b^2 = 0 \\\\ 2ab = 1 \\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>From the first equation, \\(b = \\pm a\\).\n</p><p>Case 1: \\(b = a\\)  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42b14bb18a37a1b25865ea2b35e194c11fafe19c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2a^2 = 1 \\implies a = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}, \\quad b = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Case 2: \\(b = -a\\)  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a408efaaa74911adfc57da3f7db3da29df8355.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-2a^2 = 1 \\quad \\text{(impossible for real } a\\text{)}\\]\" width=\"248\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Hence the square roots of \\(i\\) are  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9f2a45e8f1aaa048837a0e6f754308f1357d202.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}i, \\quad -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}i\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>---\n</p><p>Final Answer:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcb3dea044dc00654394b0cd8e3c7934e767e78f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Square root of himself: } 1, -1\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2ddd6a3eef306575bdf383c595c174a8454d4e5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Square roots of } i: \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}i, \\; -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}i\\]\" width=\"333\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>---\n</p><p>Bonus Joke:\n</p><p>When she said,  \n</p>\n<ul><li>\"What is the root of your incompetence?\"*</li></ul>\n<p>He replied,  \n</p>\n<ul><li>\"Well, it’s either 1 or -1… but don’t worry, I’m still trying to solve for i myself!\"* 😎</li></ul>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=~Trashboycan\" title=\"~Trashboycan\">~Trashboycan</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Advanced_Topics_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Advanced_Topics_Problems\" title=\"2006 SMT/Advanced Topics Problems\">2006 SMT/Advanced Topics Problems</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017211843\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 83/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3105/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11177:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017211843 and revision id 280579. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}